    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-efficiency plays: **Christian Yelich** (70.50) and **Yordan Alvarez** (69.65). **Christian Yelich** benefits from a distinct environmental advantage against Zebby Matthews; the projected slow delivery time from the mound boosts his stolen base upside, a critical factor for our roster\u2019s scarcity strategy, while his platoon edge adds significant lift. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start despite a challenging matchup against Robbie Ray. His elite xwOBA of 0.473 effectively mitigates the platoon disadvantage, and his placement in the two-hole provides the optimal volume to anchor our run production today.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on our middle infield, where **Caleb Durbin** (52.01) narrowly edged out **Chase Meidroth** (48.53) for the final utility spot. While **Chase Meidroth** offered a strong lead-off profile, **Caleb Durbin**\u2019s neutral platoon standing against Perkins paired with a more favorable park factor secured his position. We are closely monitoring the rain risk in the games involving **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Trea Turner**, **Carson Benge**, and **Kyle Schwarber**, as the 33\u201340% precipitation probability threatens to truncate potential production. Despite the tough assignment against Zack Wheeler, **Kazuma Okamoto** remains active due to his base projection, though he carries the most significant risk of being neutralized by Wheeler\u2019s elite arm. With **Casey Schmitt** sidelined on the IL and **Nelson Velazquez** unavailable, we are leaning heavily on the versatility of **Colt Keith** (63.10) to sustain our offensive floor should the aforementioned rain delays impact our top-tier performers.",
